<h1>Deliverables</h1>

<p class="en-start-idea">Everything the programme has deposited, in one place. The materials are open: the coding manual, the annotated corpus, the system prompt, the extraction scripts, the raw outputs of both arms and the blind packet. Anyone who wants to check a figure rather than take it on trust has what it takes to do so.</p>

<p class="en-deliv-note">Superseded versions are kept and marked rather than removed. A programme that corrects itself has to leave the corrections visible, and a reader who cited an earlier draft has to be able to find it. Each entry links to the note that introduced it, where the document is discussed.</p>

{% for key in deliverableGroups.order %}
  {% set groupDocs = collections.labDocuments | groupOf(key) %}
  {% if groupDocs.length %}
<section class="en-deliv-group" aria-label="{{ deliverableGroups.labels[key] }}">
  <h2 class="en-deliv-title">{{ deliverableGroups.labels[key] }}</h2>
  {% if deliverableGroups.notes[key] %}<p class="en-deliv-gloss">{{ deliverableGroups.notes[key] }}</p>{% endif %}

  <ul class="en-deliv-list">
    {% for doc in groupDocs %}
    <li class="en-deliv-item{% if doc.superseded %} en-deliv-item--old{% endif %}">
      <p class="en-deliv-doc">
        <a href="{{ doc.downloadUrl }}">{{ doc.label }}</a>
        {% if doc.version %}<span class="en-deliv-version">{{ doc.version }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if doc.superseded %}<span class="en-deliv-flag">superseded</span>{% endif %}
      </p>
      <p class="en-deliv-meta">{{ doc.date | formatDateEN }} &middot; introduced in <a href="{{ doc.sourceUrl }}">{{ doc.sourceTitle }}</a></p>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<p class="en-deliv-foot">The current figures, and which of them are not yet declared, are on the <a href="/lab/status/">project status page</a>. The reasoning behind each document is in the <a href="/lab/">research log</a>.</p>
